# Rust invariants

## Paths and persistence

- Runtime files: `get_data_dir().join(...)` — never hardcode `/data` or relative paths
- Persist with atomic write + rename (see `ping.rs`, memory, flight tracker)
- Baked assets in `crates/data/assets/` (CSVs via `include_str!`, flight DBs via build.rs) — no runtime file deps for prod image

## Time

- Bot scheduling / local display use `Europe/Berlin` (`util::BERLIN`, `util::to_berlin`)
- Time is `jiff` only (no `chrono`/`chrono-tz`/`humantime`, unmaintained); `jiff` uses `tzdb-bundle-always` so the musl `FROM scratch` image has the full IANA DB and Aviationstack airport timezones can reinterpret local wall times stamped as `+00:00`

## Config security

- Config structs: `Deserialize` only — **never** add `Serialize` (credential leak via debug dump)
- Secrets in `SecretString` (secrecy crate)

## IRC / handlers

- Fault is fail-fast (ADR-0012): an unexpected task exit or panic, even one command's, ends the runtime; handle operational failures inside the task (`bail!` on startup only)
- Broadcast channel capacity 100; lagging handlers continue after `RecvError::Lagged`
- Request/response on broadcast: subscribe **before** send (PING/PONG race)
- `twitch_irc::irc!` macro needs standalone `use twitch_irc::irc;`

## Resilience

- Aviation client init failure: log, disable aviation features — do not abort the bot
- Ping templates: reject control chars on create/edit (CR/LF splits PRIVMSG)

## Style

- Clippy is strict (`-D warnings`); don't `#[allow]` without a one-line reason
- Errors follow ADR-0012: typed when a caller branches, `eyre` otherwise; Surface text via `match`, never `to_string()`
- Log errors once, where handled, with `?error` not `%error` (includes backtrace)
